  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : Let $\\mathrm{P}$ be the foot of the perpendicular. P lies on a line perpendicular to $x+y=2$.\n$\\therefore$ Equation of the line on which P lies is of the form : $x-y+k=0$\nBut this line passes through $(0,0)$.\n$$\n\\therefore k=0\n$$\nHence, co-ordinates of P may be obtained by solving $x+y=2$ and $y=x$\n$$\n\\therefore x=1, y=1\n$$\nHence, $\\mathrm{P} \\equiv(1,1)$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/0hOJ1Huz-Lim9xOWC0DqV8xC3L7cbkJfY9oZvx2Uagg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
